{{#> layouts/base head-sub-title="Migration notes" page-title="Migration notes" }}

  {{#*inline "body-block"}}
    <section class="introduction">
      <p class="wide">Major releases sometimes remove deprecated APIs or change how part of the library is used. Choose your target version below, and upgrade one major version at a time if you are coming from an older release.</p>
    </section>

    <h2 id="version-9">Migrating to 9.0</h2>
    <section>
      <div class="view">
        <p>Version 9 consolidates the dedicated recipient-builder API and requires the most code changes. Start here when moving from 8.x.</p>
        <a class="button" href="migration-notes-9.0.0.html#navigation">Open the 9.0 migration guide</a>
      </div>
      <div class="side">
        <p><strong>Main work:</strong> replace removed recipient overloads, review behavior changes, then compile and exercise your message-building tests.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <h2 id="historical-migrations">Historical major migrations</h2>
    <section>
      <div class="button-group">
        <a class="button" href="migration-notes-7.0.0.html#navigation">Migrating to 7.0</a>
        <a class="button" href="migration-notes-6.0.0.html#navigation">Migrating to 6.0</a>
        <a class="button" href="migration-notes-5.0.0.html#navigation">Migrating to 5.0</a>
      </div>
      <p class="wide">If your application predates version 5, follow each major-version guide in order instead of jumping straight to the newest examples.</p>
    </section>

    <h2 id="release-history">Release history</h2>
    <section>
      <p class="wide">Use <a href="https://github.com/bbottema/simple-java-mail/releases">GitHub Releases</a> and the repository's
        <a href="https://github.com/bbottema/simple-java-mail/blob/master/RELEASE_HISTORY.md">complete release history</a> for changes that do not require dedicated migration guidance.</p>
    </section>
  {{/inline}}

{{/layouts/base}}
